00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,320
 Hi, and this lesson I will talk about choosing the right chat GPT model.

2
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:10,340
 Remember, all models can be changed or updated, so for the latest information, always

3
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:14,360
 check the official documentation.

4
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:16,360
 Let's get started!

5
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:21,120
 Chat GPT isn't just one model, it's a whole family of them.

6
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:26,520
 Each one is stronger in different areas, choosing the right model means you'll get results

7
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:30,240
 that are faster, cheaper, and more accurate.

8
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:35,720
 Some models are perfect for coding, others for writing, and others for quick answers

9
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,360
 or working with images.

10
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:44,280
 When you know which model fits your task, you save time, avoid frustration, and get better

11
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:45,680
 results overall.

12
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:51,240
 It's really about working smarter, not harder, so which model should you use?

13
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:57,200
 Oh, let's break it down by use case, for developers and technical work.

14
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:04,640
 Use GPT 5 Syncing or GPT 5 Syncing Mini for the Boggins and Data Reviews.

15
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:08,600
 Choose GPT 5 Pro for complex refactors and audits.

16
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:13,040
 Pick O3 for mass and science problem solving.

17
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:18,160
 And use GPT 5 Syncing Mini for clean snippets and lightweight coding, and for business

18
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,920
 and professionals.

19
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:25,800
 Use GPT 5 Pro for due diligence, planning, and financial or legal documents.

20
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:33,240
 Use GPT 5 Syncing for policy briefs and structured reports.

21
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:39,560
 And for fact checking the long documents, GPT 5 Syncing or GPT 5 Pro is the best choice,

22
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:43,640
 for everyday users and productivity.

23
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:48,360
 Use GPT 5 Auto for Data Mix tasks.

24
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:53,480
 Use GPT 5 Instant or GPT 5 Mini for quick answers.

25
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:58,560
 Use GPT 5 Instant for summaries, groping, and deduplication.

26
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:04,800
 And GPT 5 Syncing Mini for outlines and lightweight analysis for creators and writers.

27
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:10,640
 I know, use GPT 4.5 for long form writing with consistent tone.

28
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:17,280
 Use GPT 5 Syncing or GPT 5 Pro for detailed structured content.

29
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:23,000
 And choose GPT 4.5 or GPT 5 Pro for consistent large outputs.

30
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,240
 Finally, for visual and multi-modal work.

31
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:31,320
 Use GPT 4.0 for image analysis and reading text from pictures.

32
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:36,560
 Use GPT 4.1 for a balanced mix of multi-modal reasoning and coding.

33
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:40,160
 Pick O4 Mini for quick image and text tasks.

34
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:45,360
 And GPT 4.0 when you want to compare visuals against GPT 5 results.

35
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:49,040
 I hope this lesson was useful for you and see you in the next lesson.

